IMPORT prelude

-- Civil List and Gratuity Act 1970 (Singapore) -- the President's civil list: the yearly sums in the Schedule and who is paid them
-- (s 2), the funds charged (ss 3, 13), daily accrual and monthly payment (s 4), appropriation and moving a surplus between classes
-- (s 5), a change of holder (s 6); and the gratuity on the death of a President or former President (s 10) and its protection from
-- assignment and attachment (s 12).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 6/3/2026"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CLGA1970.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021";
-- the latest amendment annotated is the Schedule resolution S 130/2026 wef 06/03/2026. THE SCHEDULE IS COLUMN-SHIFTED IN THE .txt
-- DEPOSIT: six figures ($1,568,900, $73,000, $4,500, $7,318,000, $4,542,000, $1,288,000) appear beside six items, but displaced. They
-- were matched to the items BY ORDER OF APPEARANCE, not by line position: privy purse, entertainment allowance, acting President's
-- allowance (Class 1), salaries of personal staff (Class 2), expenses of household (Class 3), special services (Class 4). $1,568,900
-- prints on the "Class 1" heading line; it is read as the privy purse, not a Class 1 total, because there are exactly six figures
-- for six items and no other class prints a total apart from its item (inference from the layout, not stated in the text).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0161 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. The Act is short (ss 1-13, four of them repealed) and is encoded nearly whole; the only "person" it reaches
-- beyond the President and the acting President is a dead President's dependants, his personal representative, and his creditors.
-- Not encoded: s 1 (short title), s 5(3) beyond a comment (Classes 2-4 spent to Minister-approved estimates), s 7 (Parliament varies
-- the Schedule by resolution) beyond a comment, the repealed ss 8, 9, 11, and the AMOUNT of a gratuity, which the Act leaves to
-- resolution of Parliament.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil List and Gratuity Act 1970 -- civil list and gratuity`

DECLARE `Schedule item` IS ONE OF
    `the privy purse`
    `the entertainment allowance`
    `the acting President's allowance`
    `salaries of personal staff`
    `expenses of household`
    `special services`

DECLARE Payee IS ONE OF
    `the President`
    `the person exercising the functions of President under Article 22N or 22O`
    `paid by or on the instructions of the Private Secretary`

DECLARE Fund IS ONE OF
    `the Consolidated Fund`
    `the Pension Fund`

DECLARE `Kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `a civil list payment`
    `a gratuity`

DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `his dependants`
    `his legal personal representative`

DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `a debt due to the Government`
    `a maintenance order for his wife`
    `a maintenance order for his former wife`
    `a maintenance order for his minor child`
    `a maintenance order for an adult child`
    `a maintenance order for a husband`
    `a lump-sum court order`
    `a bank loan`
    `a private creditor's judgment`

§§ `The Schedule -- sums payable`

-- THE SCHEDULE. "SUMS PAYABLE". Class 1: (a) The privy purse; (b) Entertainment allowance; (c) Acting President's allowance.
-- Class 2: Salaries of personal staff. Class 3: Expenses of household. Class 4: Special services.
-- [S 130/2026 wef 06/03/2026] [S 126/2023 wef 06/03/2023]. Figures matched by order -- see the header.
-- s 2(1): "the yearly sums specified in the Schedule".
GIVEN `the item` IS A `Schedule item`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the yearly sum` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `the privy purse` THEN 1568900
    WHEN `the entertainment allowance` THEN 73000
    WHEN `the acting President's allowance` THEN 4500
    WHEN `salaries of personal staff` THEN 7318000
    WHEN `expenses of household` THEN 4542000
    WHEN `special services` THEN 1288000

GIVEN `the item` IS A `Schedule item`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the class of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `the privy purse` THEN 1
    WHEN `the entertainment allowance` THEN 1
    WHEN `the acting President's allowance` THEN 1
    WHEN `salaries of personal staff` THEN 2
    WHEN `expenses of household` THEN 3
    WHEN `special services` THEN 4

GIVEN `class number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the class total` MEANS
    IF `class number` EQUALS 1
    THEN `the yearly sum` `the privy purse` PLUS `the yearly sum` `the entertainment allowance`
         PLUS `the yearly sum` `the acting President's allowance`
    ELSE IF `class number` EQUALS 2 THEN `the yearly sum` `salaries of personal staff`
         ELSE IF `class number` EQUALS 3 THEN `the yearly sum` `expenses of household`
              ELSE IF `class number` EQUALS 4 THEN `the yearly sum` `special services`
                   ELSE 0

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the whole civil list` MEANS
    `the class total` 1 PLUS `the class total` 2 PLUS `the class total` 3 PLUS `the class total` 4

§§ `2 -- who is paid, and not during a vacancy`

-- s 2(2): "Payments in respect of the amounts for the privy purse and entertainment allowance specified in Class 1 of the Schedule
-- shall be made to the President."
-- (3): "Payments of the acting President's allowance ... shall be made to the person exercising the functions of the office of
-- President pursuant to Article 22N or 22O of the Constitution."
-- (4): Classes 2, 3 and 4 "shall be made by or on the instructions of the Private Secretary to the President in accordance with any
-- written law governing the disbursement of public funds".
GIVEN `the item` IS A `Schedule item`
GIVETH A Payee
`who is paid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `the privy purse` THEN `the President`
    WHEN `the entertainment allowance` THEN `the President`
    WHEN `the acting President's allowance` THEN `the person exercising the functions of President under Article 22N or 22O`
    OTHERWISE `paid by or on the instructions of the Private Secretary`

-- s 2(1): paid "so long as he holds office".
-- (5): "No payment in respect of the amounts specified in Class 1 of the Schedule shall be made in respect of any period during which
-- the office of the President is vacant."
-- Read literally, (5) bars the acting President's allowance too, since it is a Class 1 item -- even though (3) directs it to whoever
-- acts under Article 22N or 22O. Whether either Article covers a vacancy is a matter of the Constitution, which was not read here.
-- Classes 2-4 are not barred by (5): the household and staff go on being paid.
GIVEN `the item` IS A `Schedule item`, `the office is vacant for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a payment may be made for the period` IF
    (NOT (`the class of` `the item` EQUALS 1)) OR (NOT `the office is vacant for the period`)

§§ `3 and 13 -- which fund pays`

-- s 3: "The sums required for payments under section 2 shall be charged on and paid out of the Consolidated Fund."
-- s 13: gratuities "charged on and paid out of the Pension Fund established by the Pension Fund Act 1995".
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of payment`
GIVETH A Fund
`the fund charged` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a civil list payment` THEN `the Consolidated Fund`
    WHEN `a gratuity` THEN `the Pension Fund`

§§ `4 and 6 -- accrual, payday and a change of holder`

-- s 4: "The yearly sums payable under Class 1 of the Schedule shall -- (a) accrue from day to day; and (b) be payable monthly on the
-- last day of each month or on such other day as the Minister may from time to time determine."
-- The Act does not say how a yearly sum is divided into days. The divisor is taken here as a parameter (365 or 366) -- an
-- inference. No rounding is modelled; the cases use periods that give whole dollars.
GIVEN `the item` IS A `Schedule item`, `days` IS A NUMBER, `days in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum accrued` MEANS
    IF `the class of` `the item` EQUALS 1
    THEN `the yearly sum` `the item` TIMES `days` DIVIDED BY `days in the year`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `the day of the month` IS A NUMBER, `the last day of the month` IS A NUMBER,
      `the Minister has determined another day` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister's day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Class 1 is payable on that day` IF
    IF `the Minister has determined another day`
    THEN `the day of the month` EQUALS `the Minister's day`
    ELSE `the day of the month` EQUALS `the last day of the month`

-- s 6: "In the event of there being a change of holder of the office of President, there shall be made such adjustments and
-- distribution of the annual payment due under section 2 in respect of the amounts specified for Class 1 of the Schedule as the
-- circumstances of the case may require."
-- The Act fixes no formula. Splitting by days held, using the s 4(a) daily accrual, is an INFERENCE.
GIVEN `the item` IS A `Schedule item`, `days held by the outgoing holder` IS A NUMBER, `days in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the incoming holder's share` MEANS
    `the sum accrued` `the item` (`days in the year` MINUS `days held by the outgoing holder`) `days in the year`

§§ `5 -- appropriation, and moving a surplus between classes`

-- s 5(1): the Schedule amounts "shall be appropriated to the classes of expenditure specified therein respectively in that year".
-- (2): "If it appears that the sum appropriated to any class of expenditure in any year will not be wholly required for the
-- expenditure of that class in that year, the amount not so required may, with the approval of the Minister, be applied as an
-- addition to the sum available for any other class."
-- (3): Classes 2-4 to be spent "in conformity with the detailed estimates for that year submitted by him to, and approved by, the
-- Minister" (not encoded beyond this comment).
-- "any class" is not limited to Classes 2-4: read literally, an unneeded part of Class 1 may be moved too.
GIVEN `the sum appropriated` IS A NUMBER, `the sum required` IS A NUMBER, `the Minister approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount that may be moved to another class` MEANS
    IF `the Minister approves` AND `the sum required` LESS THAN `the sum appropriated`
    THEN `the sum appropriated` MINUS `the sum required`
    ELSE 0

§§ `10 -- gratuity on death`

-- s 10: "Where, after 1 July 1970, the President or a former President dies, there may be paid to his dependants or, if there are no
-- dependants, to his legal personal representative a gratuity of such amount as Parliament may by resolution determine."
-- "may": the gratuity is discretionary. Its amount is not in the Act.
GIVEN `was President or a former President` IS A BOOLEAN, `died after 1 July 1970` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a gratuity may be paid` IF
    `was President or a former President` AND `died after 1 July 1970`

GIVEN `there are dependants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Recipient
`the gratuity goes to` MEANS
    IF `there are dependants` THEN `his dependants` ELSE `his legal personal representative`

§§ `12 -- not assignable, not attachable`

-- s 12: a gratuity "shall not be -- (a) assignable or transferable except for the purpose of satisfying -- (i) a debt due to the
-- Government; or (ii) an order of any court for the payment of periodical sums of money towards the maintenance of the wife, or
-- former wife or minor child of the former President to whom the gratuity has been granted; and (b) attached, sequestered or levied
-- upon for or in respect of any debt or claim whatever except a debt due to the Government."
-- The text names a wife, former wife or minor child; a husband is not named. A lump-sum order is not "periodical sums".
GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gratuity may be assigned to satisfy` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a debt due to the Government` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a maintenance order for his wife` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a maintenance order for his former wife` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a maintenance order for his minor child` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- (b): only a debt due to the Government. A maintenance order may be satisfied by assignment under (a)(ii) but cannot be enforced by
-- attachment under (b).
GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gratuity may be attached for` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a debt due to the Government` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
